From a99d859eb2fddbcb4edc159ab8a695c051429ac6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meson Codec <meson-codec@localhost>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 20:43:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: add H.264 P-frame and GOP state

Keep two reconstructed Canvas buffers as alternating current and reference
frames. Track frame_num, picture order count and IDR identifiers across
jobs, and submit the GXL NON_IDR command for frames inside a GOP.

Expose fixed Baseline, level and header capabilities plus standard GOP,
I/P QP and force-keyframe controls. Register the M2M media-controller
topology and encoder commands so userspace can identify and control a
stateful encoder.

The GXL full microcode reports IDR_DONE for both IDR and NON_IDR frame
commands. Distinguish them using the submitted command, returned NAL type
and V4L2 buffer flags.

Signed-off-by: Meson Codec <meson-codec@localhost>
---
 .../platform/amlogic/meson-venc/meson-venc.c  | 253 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 234 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/meson-venc/meson-venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/meson-venc/meson-venc.c
index ddcf956..29b8999 100644
